# Lecture 11D

## Chromosome Alterations: Deletions

## Chapter 9

## Dr. Neil Voss

## November 17, 2026

=== layout: bookend

# Learning Objectives

@body

- Distinguish the four chromosome rearrangements.
- Explain how deletions uncover recessive alleles.
- Infer gene order from overlapping deletions.
- Check a proposed order against every deletion.

=== layout: section

# Alterations of Chromosome Structure

=== layout: one-panel

# *Alterations of Chromosome Structure*

@body

- Breakage of a chromosome can lead to four types of changes in chromosome structure
  - [*Deletion*]{underline=true} removes a chromosomal segment
  - [*Duplication*]{underline=true} repeats a segment
  - [*Inversion*]{underline=true} reverses orientation of a segment within a chromosome
  - [*Translocation*]{underline=true} moves a segment from one chromosome to another

